- true: The file automatically parses the code.
- false: The file does not automatically parse the code.

This parameter corresponds to the **Code Parsing** setting when **Same Cycle** is selected in **Schedule Configuration > Scheduling Dependencies** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='true', position='Body'),
  autoRerunIntervalMillis?: int32(name='AutoRerunIntervalMillis', description='The interval between automatic reruns after an error occurs. Unit: milliseconds. Maximum value: 1800000, which indicates 30 minutes.

This parameter corresponds to the **Rerun Interval** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Time Attributes > Automatic Rerun after Error** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).
The time unit for the **Rerun Interval** setting in the console is minutes. Make sure to convert the time when you call this operation.', example='120000', position='Body'),
  autoRerunTimes?: int32(name='AutoRerunTimes', description='The number of automatic reruns after an error occurs. Maximum value: 10.', example='3', position='Body'),
  connectionName?: string(name='ConnectionName', description='The data source connected when the task is run after the file is deployed.
You can call the [UpdateDataSource](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/211432.html) operation to obtain the list of available data sources for the workspace.', example='odps_source', position='Body'),
  content?: string(name='Content', description='The code content of the file. The code format varies based on the file type. You can find a task of the corresponding type in Operation Center, right-click the task, and select View Code to view the specific code format.', example='SHOW TABLES;', position='Body'),
  createFolderIfNotExists?: boolean(name='CreateFolderIfNotExists', description='Specifies whether to enable automatic creation of the directory specified by the FileFolderPath parameter if it does not exist in the system. Valid values:

- true: Enables automatic creation of the directory if it does not exist.
- false: The call fails if the directory does not exist.', example='false', position='Body'),
  cronExpress?: string(name='CronExpress', description='The cron expression for periodic scheduling. This parameter corresponds to the **cron Expression** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Time Property > cron Expression** for a data development node in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console). After you configure the **Schedule Cycle** and **timed scheduling** time, DataWorks automatically generates the corresponding cron expression.

Examples:
- Schedule the task at 05:30 every day: `00 30 05 * * ?`

- Schedule the task at the 15th minute of every hour: `00 15 00-23/1 * * ?`

- Schedule the task every 10 minutes: `00 00/10 * * * ?`

- Schedule the task every 10 minutes from 08:00 to 17:00 every day: `00 00-59/10 8-17 * * * ?`

- Schedule the task at 00:20 on the first day of every month: `00 20 00 1 * ?`

- Schedule the task every three months starting from 00:10 on January 1: `00 10 00 1 1-12/3 ?`

- Schedule the task at 00:05 every Tuesday and Friday: `00 05 00 * * 2,5`

Due to the rules of the DataWorks scheduling system, the cron expression has the following limits:

- The minimum scheduling interval is 5 minutes.

- The earliest scheduling time of a day is 00:05.', example='00 05 00 * * ?', position='Body'),
  cycleType?: string(name='CycleType', description='The type of the scheduling cycle. Valid values: NOT_DAY (minute or hour) and DAY (day, week, or month).

This parameter corresponds to the **Schedule Cycle** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Time Attributes > Schedule Cycle** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='DAY', position='Body'),
  dependentNodeIdList?: string(name='DependentNodeIdList', description='The list of nodes that the current node depends on in the previous cycle.', example='abc', position='Body'),
  dependentType?: string(name='DependentType', description='The dependency on the previous cycle. Valid values:
- SELF: Depends on the current node.
- CHILD: Depends on the first-level child nodes.
- USER_DEFINE: Depends on other nodes.
- NONE: Does not depend on the previous cycle.   
- USER_DEFINE_AND_SELF: Depends on a combination of the current node and other nodes across cycles.
- CHILD_AND_SELF: Depends on a combination of the first-level child nodes and the current node across cycles.', example='NONE', position='Body'),
  endEffectDate?: long(name='EndEffectDate', description='The timestamp in milliseconds when automatic scheduling stops.

This parameter corresponds to the end time in the **Effective Date** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Time Attributes > Effective Date** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console). The value is a timestamp in milliseconds.', example='1671694850000', minimum=0, position='Body'),
  fileDescription?: string(name='FileDescription', description='The description of the file.', example='This is the file description', maxLength=200, position='Body'),
  fileFolderPath?: string(name='FileFolderPath', description='The path of the file.', example='Business_process/First_Business_Process/MaxCompute/Folder_1/Folder_2', position='Body'),
  fileName: string(name='FileName', description='The name of the file.

This parameter is required.', example='File name', position='Body'),
  fileType: int32(name='FileType', description='The code type of the file.
The code format varies based on the file type. For more information, see [DataWorks node types](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/600169.html).

You can call the [ListFileType](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/212428.html) operation to query the code type of the file.

This parameter is required.', example='10', position='Body'),
  ignoreParentSkipRunningProperty?: boolean(name='IgnoreParentSkipRunningProperty', description='Specifies whether to inherit the dry-run property from the previous cycle. Valid values:

- true: Inherit the dry-run property from the previous cycle.

- false: Do not inherit the dry-run property from the previous cycle.', example='false', position='Body'),
  imageId?: string(name='ImageId', description='The ID of the custom image.', example='m-bp1h4b5a8ogkbll2f3tr', position='Body'),
  inputList?: string(name='InputList', description='The output names of the upstream files on which the current file depends. Separate multiple output names with commas (,).

This parameter corresponds to the **Parent Node Output Name** setting when **Same Cycle** is selected in **Schedule Configuration > Scheduling Dependencies** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='project_root,project.file1,project.001_out', position='Body'),
  inputParameters?: string(name='InputParameters', description='The context input parameters of the node. The value is in JSON format. For the included fields, refer to the InputContextParameterList parameter structure in the response of the [GetFile](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173954.html) operation.

This parameter corresponds to the **Input Parameters of Current Node** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Node Context** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='[{"ValueSource": "project_001.first_node:bizdate_param","ParameterName": "bizdate_input"}]', position='Body'),
  outputList?: string(name='OutputList', description='The output names of the file. Separate multiple output names with commas (,). This parameter corresponds to the **Output Name of Current Node** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Scheduling Dependencies** for a data development task.', example='project_root,project.file1,project.001_out', position='Body'),
  outputParameters?: string(name='OutputParameters', description='The context output parameters of the node. The value is in JSON format. For the included fields, refer to the OutputContextParameterList parameter structure in the response of the [GetFile](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173954.html) operation.

This parameter corresponds to the **Output Parameters of Current Node** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Node Context** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='[{"Type": 1,"Value": "${bizdate}","ParameterName": "bizdate_param"}]', position='Body'),
  owner?: string(name='Owner', description='The Alibaba Cloud user ID of the file owner. If this parameter is left empty, the Alibaba Cloud user ID of the caller is used by default.', example='1000000000001', position='Body'),
  paraValue?: string(name='ParaValue', description='The scheduling parameters. Separate multiple parameters with spaces. 

This parameter corresponds to the **Parameters** setting in **Schedule Configuration > Parameters** for a data development task in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console). For more information, see [Scheduling parameters](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/137548.html).', example='a=x b=y', position='Body'),
