- PAUSE(2): The instance is a frozen node. The scheduling system regularly runs the instance but sets the status of the instance to failed when the scheduling system starts to run the instance.
- SKIP(3): The instance is a dry-run node. The scheduling system regularly runs the instance but sets the status of the instance to successful when the scheduling system starts to run the instance.
- SKIP_UNCHOOSE(4): The instance is an unselected node in a temporary workflow. This type of node exists only in temporary workflows. The scheduling system sets the status of the instance to successful when the scheduling system starts to run the instance.
- SKIP_CYCLE(5): The instance is a node that is scheduled by week or month and is waiting for the scheduling time to arrive. The scheduling system regularly runs the instance but sets the status of the instance to successful when the scheduling system starts to run the instance.
- CONDITION_UNCHOOSE(6): The instance is not selected by its ancestor branch node and is run as a dry-run node.
- REALTIME_DEPRECATED(7): The instance is an expired scheduled instance generated in real time. The scheduling system sets the status of the instance to successful.', example='MANUAL'),
