This parameter corresponds to the Advanced Settings section in the right-side navigation pane of the edit page for EMR Spark Streaming and EMR Streaming SQL data development tasks in the DataWorks console.

Only EMR Spark Streaming and EMR Streaming SQL tasks support this parameter. The parameter value must be in JSON format.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='{"queue":"default","SPARK_CONF":"--conf spark.driver.memory=2g"}', position='Body'),
  applyScheduleImmediately?: boolean(name='ApplyScheduleImmediately', description='Specifies whether the scheduling configurations take effect immediately after the file is deployed.', example='true', position='Body'),
  autoParsing?: boolean(name='AutoParsing', description='Specifies whether to enable the automatic parsing feature for the file. Valid values:
- true: The file automatically parses code.
- false: The file does not automatically parse code.

This parameter corresponds to the Code Parsing option in the Schedule Settings > Scheduling Dependencies > Same Cycle section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='true', position='Body'),
  autoRerunIntervalMillis?: int32(name='AutoRerunIntervalMillis', description='The interval for automatic reruns after an error occurs. Unit: milliseconds. Maximum value: 1800000, which equals 30 minutes.

This parameter corresponds to the Rerun Interval parameter in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Automatic Rerun after Error section of the DataWorks console.
The unit of the Rerun Interval parameter in the console is minutes. Convert the time unit when you call this operation.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='120000', position='Body'),
  autoRerunTimes?: int32(name='AutoRerunTimes', description='The number of automatic reruns after an error occurs.', example='3', position='Body'),
  connectionName?: string(name='ConnectionName', description='The identifier of the data source used by the task when the task corresponding to the file is run. You can call the [ListDataSources](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/211431.html) operation to obtain the list of available data sources.', example='odps_source', position='Body'),
  content?: string(name='Content', description='The code content of the file. The code format varies based on the file type. You can go to Operation Center, right-click a task of the corresponding type, and select View Code to view the specific code format.', example='SELECT "1";', position='Body'),
  cronExpress?: string(name='CronExpress', description='The cron expression for periodic scheduling. This parameter corresponds to the Cron Expression parameter in the Schedule > Time Property > Cron Expression section of the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console). After you configure the scheduling cycle and scheduled time, DataWorks automatically generates the corresponding cron expression.

Examples:

- Schedule a node at 05:30 every day: `00 30 05 * * ?`.

- Schedule a node at the 15th minute of every hour: `00 15 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node every 10 minutes: `00 00/10 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node every 10 minutes from 08:00 to 17:00 every day: `00 00-59/10 8-23 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node at 00:20 on the first day of every month: `00 20 00 1 * ?`.

- Schedule a node every three months starting from 00:10 on January 1: `00 10 00 1 1-12/3 ?`.

- Schedule a node at 00:05 every Tuesday and Friday: `00 05 00 * * 2,5`.

Due to the rules of the DataWorks scheduling system, cron expressions have the following limits:

- The minimum scheduling interval is 5 minutes.

- The earliest scheduling time of a day is 00:05.', example='00 00-59/5 1-23 * * ?', position='Body'),
  cycleType?: string(name='CycleType', description='The type of the scheduling cycle. Valid values: NOT_DAY (minute and hour) and DAY (day, week, and month).

This parameter corresponds to the Scheduling Cycle parameter in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Scheduling Cycle section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='NOT_DAY', position='Body'),
  dependentNodeIdList?: string(name='DependentNodeIdList', description='The IDs of the nodes on which the current file depends. This parameter is used to specify the dependent node IDs when the DependentType parameter is set to USER_DEFINE. Separate multiple node IDs with commas (,).

This parameter corresponds to the content configured when the Schedule Settings > Scheduling Dependencies parameter is set to Previous Cycle and the dependent item is set to Other Nodes for a data development node in the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console).', example='5,10,15,20', position='Body'),
  dependentType?: string(name='DependentType', description='The dependency on the previous cycle. Valid values:
- SELF: The node depends on itself.
- CHILD: The node depends on its level-1 child nodes.
- USER_DEFINE: The node depends on other nodes.
- NONE: The node does not depend on the previous cycle.', example='USER_DEFINE', position='Body'),
  endEffectDate?: long(name='EndEffectDate', description='The timestamp in milliseconds when automatic scheduling stops.

This parameter corresponds to the end time of the Effective Date parameter in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Effective Date section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='4155787800000', minimum=0, position='Body'),
  fileDescription?: string(name='FileDescription', description='The description of the file.', example='Here is the file description', maxLength=200, position='Body'),
  fileFolderPath?: string(name='FileFolderPath', description='The path of the file.', example='Business_process/First_Business_Process/data_integration/Folder_1/Folder_2', position='Body'),
  fileId: long(name='FileId', description='The ID of the file. You can call the [ListFiles](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173942.html) operation to obtain the file ID.

This parameter is required.', example='100000001', position='Body'),
  fileName?: string(name='FileName', description='The name of the file. You can change the file name by resetting the value of FileName.
For example, you can call the [ListFiles](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173942.html) operation to query the ID of a file in the destination directory, and then call the [UpdateFile](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173951.html) operation. Set the FileId parameter to the queried file ID and specify the FileName parameter to change the name of the file.', example='ods_user_info_d', position='Body'),
  ignoreParentSkipRunningProperty?: boolean(name='IgnoreParentSkipRunningProperty', description='Specifies whether to skip the dry-run property of upstream nodes in the previous cycle.', example='true', position='Body'),
  imageId?: string(name='ImageId', description='The ID of the custom image.', example='m-uf6d7npxk1hhek8ng0cb', position='Body'),
  inputList?: string(name='InputList', description='The output names of the upstream files on which the current file depends. Separate multiple output names with commas (,).

This parameter corresponds to the Parent Node Output Name parameter in the Schedule Settings > Scheduling Dependencies > Same Cycle section of the DataWorks console.

> This parameter is required when you create a batch synchronization task by calling the CreateDISyncTask and UpdateFile operations.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='project_root,project.file1,project.001_out', position='Body'),
  inputParameters?: string(name='InputParameters', description='The context input parameters of the node. The parameter value must be in JSON format. For the fields included, refer to the InputContextParameterList parameter structure in the response of the [GetFile](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173954.html) operation.

This parameter corresponds to the Input Parameters of Current Node parameter in the Schedule Settings > Node Context > Input Parameters section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='[{"ValueSource": "project_001.first_node:bizdate_param","ParameterName": "bizdate_input"}]', position='Body'),
  outputList?: string(name='OutputList', description='The output of the file.

This parameter corresponds to the Output Name of Current Node parameter in the Schedule Settings > Scheduling Dependencies > Same Cycle section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='dw_project.ods_user_info_d', position='Body'),
  outputParameters?: string(name='OutputParameters', description='The context output parameters of the node. The parameter value must be in JSON format. For the fields included, refer to the OutputContextParameterList parameter structure in the response of the [GetFile](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173954.html) operation.

This parameter corresponds to the Output Parameters of Current Node parameter in the Schedule Settings > Node Context > Output Parameters section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='[{"Type": 1,"Value": "${bizdate}","ParameterName": "bizdate_param"}]', position='Body'),
  owner?: string(name='Owner', description='The user ID of the file owner.', example='18023848927592', position='Body'),
  paraValue?: string(name='ParaValue', description='The scheduling parameters.

This parameter corresponds to the Parameters section in the Schedule Settings > Parameters section of the DataWorks console. For more information, see [Scheduling parameters](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/137548.html).
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='x=a y=b z=c', position='Body'),
  projectId?: long(name='ProjectId', description='The ID of the DataWorks workspace. You can log on to the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console) and go to the workspace management page to obtain the ID.', example='100001', position='Body'),
  projectIdentifier?: string(name='ProjectIdentifier', description='The name of the DataWorks workspace. You can log on to the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console) and go to the Workspace Configuration page to obtain the workspace name.

You must specify either this parameter or the ProjectId parameter to determine the DataWorks workspace for this API call.', example='dw_project', position='Body'),
  rerunMode?: string(name='RerunMode', description='The rerun mode. Valid values:
- ALL_ALLOWED: The node can be rerun regardless of whether it is successfully run or fails to run.
- FAILURE_ALLOWED: The node cannot be rerun if it is successfully run, but can be rerun if it fails to run.
- ALL_DENIED: The node cannot be rerun regardless of whether it is successfully run or fails to run.

This parameter corresponds to the Rerun Mode parameter in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Rerun Mode section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='ALL_ALLOWED', position='Body'),
  resourceGroupIdentifier?: string(name='ResourceGroupIdentifier', description='The resource group used to run the task after the file is deployed as a task. You can call the [ListResourceGroups](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/173913.html) operation to obtain the list of available resource groups in the workspace.', example='default_group', position='Body'),
  schedulerType?: string(name='SchedulerType', description='The scheduling type. Valid values:
- NORMAL: Normal scheduling task.
- MANUAL: Manual task. The task is not run on a daily schedule and corresponds to a node in a manual workflow.
- PAUSE: Paused task.
- SKIP: Dry-run task. The task is run on a daily schedule, but its status is directly set to successful when the scheduling is started.', example='NORMAL', position='Body'),
  startEffectDate?: long(name='StartEffectDate', description='The timestamp in milliseconds when automatic scheduling starts.

This parameter corresponds to the start time of the Effective Date parameter in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Effective Date section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='936923400000', minimum=0, position='Body'),
  startImmediately?: boolean(name='StartImmediately', description='Specifies whether to start the task immediately after it is deployed. Valid values:
- true: Start the task immediately after it is deployed.
- false: Do not start the task immediately after it is deployed.

This parameter corresponds to the Start Mode parameter in the Configuration > Time Attributes > Start Mode section in the right-side navigation pane of the edit page for EMR Spark Streaming and EMR Streaming SQL data development tasks in the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='true', position='Body'),
  stop?: boolean(name='Stop', description='Specifies whether to pause scheduling. Valid values:
- true: Pause scheduling.
- false: Do not pause scheduling.

This parameter corresponds to the Pause Scheduling option in the Schedule Settings > Time Attributes > Schedule Type section of the DataWorks console.
[DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console)', example='false', position='Body'),
  timeout?: int32(name='Timeout', description='The timeout definition in the scheduling configurations.', example='1', position='Body'),
}

